@page "/"

<GalleryPage Title="Gallery">
    <Lede>Every component of FluentCMS Components on a page of its own, in each of the three render modes of Blazor. It is the documentation of the library and the target of its browser tests.</Lede>

    <Section Title="Render modes">
        <p>Every page runs in static server-side rendering, in interactive server mode and in interactive WebAssembly mode. The address says which: <code>/static/tokens</code>, <code>/server/tokens</code> and <code>/wasm/tokens</code> are one page. The first switch in the header opens the page in view in another mode.</p>
        <p>The gallery sets the mode, in one place. The library never does, and no page names one. <PageLink Page="render-modes">The sample page</PageLink> shows the difference.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section Title="Theme, density and direction">
        <p>The other switches set <code>data-fl-theme</code>, <code>data-fl-density</code> and <code>dir</code> on the root of the page. They are links, so they work where no code runs, and the choice stays in the address from page to page:</p>
        <Example Code="/static/tokens?theme=dark&density=compact&dir=rtl" />
        <p><PageLink Page="tokens">The tokens</PageLink> show what each of them changes.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section Title="Levels">
        <p>Each component declares one of three levels, shown under the title of its page.</p>
        <div class="gallery-scroll">
            <table class="gallery-table">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">Level</th>
                        <th scope="col">Meaning</th>
                        <th scope="col">Examples</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Static</td><td>Markup and CSS. It works fully with no code running.</td><td>Button, card, badge, navigation</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Native</td><td>Its behaviour comes from native elements and the script of the library. It works fully in static server-side rendering.</td><td>Dialog, menu, tabs, disclosure</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Interactive</td><td>It needs an interactive render mode for its full function, and renders a static fallback where there is none.</td><td>Table with sorting, combobox, tree</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </Section>

    <Section Title="Pages">
        <ul>
            @foreach (GalleryPageInfo entry in GalleryPages.All.Skip(1))
            {
                <li><PageLink Page="@entry.Path">@entry.Title</PageLink></li>
            }
        </ul>
        <p>A component gets its page when it is built. Until then its drawing, with every variant and state, is in the <a class="fl-link" href="https://github.com/fluentcms/FluentCMS.Components/tree/main/design/system">design system</a>.</p>
    </Section>
</GalleryPage>
